// The foothills between the lowland biomes and the mountains, so the ranges
// rise out of hills rather than out of a flat plain. The window runs up
// under the mountains' (ticket 0004, step 2): with the ranges tens of
// kilometres apart (35 km in that step, 47.5 km and long lines since its
// step 2b) the band where a range's flank climbs is a few kilometres wide,
// and all of it is foothills rather than a thin ring round a range. It
// starts no lower than 0.64 because hot, wet lowland fits no lowland biome
// and falls to the coast, whose only rival there is this window: from 0.62
// the foothills' hills bled into that coast, Port Serein's included, by a
// fifth. The relief is taller and closer-set than a lowland's so that the
// foothills are hills of their own (a mean relief slope of 11 degrees); at
// 500 m it lifted plains on the foothills' edge over the 400 m the plains
// are held to (`tests/coverage.rs`). The top of the window, 0.82, is where
// the mountains take over: with theirs from 0.80 the two part at 0.81, and
// the mountains stand alone from 0.85; their relief starts to rise from
// 0.79 (`WorldParams::mountain_rise_lead`). Up a range's flank this relief
// lies down (`WorldParams::flank_damping`), and a province may give it
// another shape (`assets/geology/`, ticket 0004, step 4).
(
    id: "strata:highlands",
    name: "Highlands",
    climate: (
        temperature: (min: 0.0, max: 1.0),
        moisture: (min: 0.0, max: 1.0),
        elevation: (min: 0.64, max: 0.82),
    ),
    relief: (kind: "hills", amplitude_m: 450.0, wavelength_m: 2000.0, octaves: 4, lift_m: 60.0, erosion: 0.8),
    surface: (material: "strata:grass", slope_material: "strata:rock", slope_threshold: 0.45),
    tint: (0.40, 0.50, 0.28),
    // The ground's palette colour (ticket 0006): a cooler, bluer green than the lowland's.
    ground: (0.42, 0.52, 0.40),
    // Between the plains and the peaks: a little of the plains' green
    // and clearer brights, no warmth.
    grade: (tint: -0.003, gain: 1.02),
)
